{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKPMyNaPaC9wu2sPPfwM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E5XAkEv6tYEevVhLZZteeE","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app","since":"2026-04-16","path":"src","perPage":100},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":13425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":388},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf239c98-82bb-4f65-bf02-8aacaa0b7f69","uuid":"386b8647-c956-48d2-afa4-400f4db27430","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:13:50.839Z","request_id":"req_011CgKPMy6iMd3cYinCGfZ5s","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01E5XAkEv6tYEevVhLZZteeE":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app","since":"2026-04-16","path":"src","perPage":100}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E5XAkEv6tYEevVhLZZteeE","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5XAkEv6tYEevVhLZZteeE","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c770afca8921295dd87d8e7c185a8a4fef231376\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T18:15:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6112: Create bill / Add bill items workspace should show which patient is being billed in tablet mode (#885)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD\",\"body\":\"* O3-6112: Billing Create bill / Add bill items workspace doesn't show which patient is being billed\\n\\n* O3-6112: Keep billing form fields directly under patient header\\n\\n* (fix) O3-6112: Show patient header in billing form workspace on tablet only\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Juliet wamalwa <julietwamalwa@Juliets-MacBook-Air.local>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0fc74eec7e4432d8ec733c6a9e21f19239ff3740\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T07:47:23+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use the framework PageHeader for the billing headers (#869)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"BillingHeader rebuilt the framework's PageHeader by hand, with its own\\nreceipt illustration, a hardcoded \\\"Billing\\\" label above the title, and\\nthe title in a p. Render PageHeader and PageHeaderContent instead, with\\nthe framework's PaymentsDeskPictogram, so billing picks up the same\\nheader as the rest of O3: the configured implementation name above the\\ntitle, and framework fixes such as the title rendering as a heading.\\n\\nThe billing dashboard's title changes from \\\"Home\\\" to \\\"Billing\\\", since\\n\\\"Billing\\\" no longer appears above it. The administration page keeps\\n\\\"Billing administration\\\". The header doesn't shrink in the\\nadministration page's flex layout, and the unused illustration and\\n\\\"home\\\" translation are removed.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e90bcf41f5e898ad3ca6d32ede21a515a86be639\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T01:24:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Highlight the active billing settings menu item (#874)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Marks the Billing settings submenu item for the current page as active.\\nThe items were never passed `isActive`, so neither Cash point\\nconfiguration nor Payment modes configuration was highlighted while it\\nwas open. The path check is the same one the Billable services,\\nDiscount requests and Refund requests links already use.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d7709b45a79100e07ba5eb03ab0e4a071ae11bb1\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T16:59:54+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Remove leftover workspace v1 container (#857)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Removes the v1 WorkspaceContainer from the billable services home page.\\nThe billing app already uses workspace v2, which the app shell renders on\\nits own, so the container renders nothing today.\\n\\nopenmrs-esm-core#1893 removes WorkspaceContainer from the framework. Once\\nthat ships, the import resolves to undefined and rendering it crashes the\\nbillable services page.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e021519623779cdf5f866fa0541aecfdbcc4aeaa\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T12:05:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Load billing pages, forms and modals only when they open (#854)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Load billing pages, forms and modals only when they open\\n\\nRegister the billing dashboard, billable services page, bill history,\\nvisit check-in form and the seven modals that used getSyncLifecycle with\\ngetAsyncLifecycle instead, so their code only loads when they're shown.\\n\\nWith getSyncLifecycle, all of them were part of the code the module loads\\nas soon as it starts, and the Billing link on the home page starts the\\nmodule. So every session downloaded billing's invoice and forms, along\\nwith zod, react-hook-form and react-to-print, before anyone opened\\nanything billing-related. The module now loads 67 KiB up front instead of\\n297 KiB. The nav links, left panel links and patient banner tags stay\\nsynchronous because they render on other apps' pages.\\n\\n* Share react-router-dom with the app shell\\n\\nAdd react-router-dom to peerDependencies, so billing uses the copy the app\\nshell provides.\\n\\nWithout it, billing bundled and loaded its own copy of react-router-dom,\\nreact-router and @remix-run/router (about 14 KiB), even though the app\\nshell already shares them.\\n\\n* Remove the unused billable services app menu item\\n\\nRemove the billableServicesAppMenuItem extension, its routes.json entry\\nand the menu item component. It was registered in app-menu-item-slot,\\nwhich nothing in the reference application renders. The app menu\\nrenders app-menu-slot, and billable services is still reachable from\\nits System Administration card.\\n\\nThe item was added in #42 for UgandaEMR's app search, which does render\\napp-menu-item-slot, but UgandaEMR now ships its own billing fork\\n(@epcare/esm-billing-app) with its own copy of this extension. The\\n\\\"Billable services\\\" string is still used elsewhere, so the translations\\ndon't change.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6e4cdcd9db634a947b317df793d5b8170a9768e9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T20:43:12+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add date range filter to bills table (#831)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add date range filter to bills table\\n\\n* (feat) Guard inverted date range and show Clear dates only when a date is set\\n\\nSkip the bill fetch when the end date is before the start date and show\\nthe picker's invalid text instead, since the backend rejects that range\\nwith a 400. Render the Clear dates button only when a date is set. Raise\\nthe billing backend floor to 2.5.0-0, which is the version that adds the\\nstartDate and endDate search parameters.\\n\\n* (fix) Skip the bills request for an inverted date range and let the date controls wrap\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"64f5bc47dcd899995e7c60f68712503bc816e939\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T18:39:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Billing app shouldn't generate global CSS rules (#830)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"37f1d48ba37e2e673e90259a086b56ccaf588e81\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T19:12:07+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#808)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace the legacy ESLint configuration with the shared flat config at version 2.0.0. Preserve type-aware export linting and repository-specific rule behavior, remove redundant lint dependencies, and apply the resulting e2e and source cleanups.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4609dcbbcb3a438a135aa3af7c8b0eaf1aa85927\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T02:13:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Shorten the billing admin card copy so it fits its tile\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The billing card on the system administration page used a long\\ndescription, Billable services, cash points, payment modes, discounts,\\nand refunds, as its content line. The admin card tiles have a fixed\\nheight with the arrow icon absolutely positioned in the bottom right\\ncorner, so the three line description overlapped the icon and ran into\\nthe bottom edge of the tile.\\n\\nThe card now follows the pattern the other admin cards use, where the\\nheading is a Manage <domain> category and the content is the name of\\nthe destination: Manage billing over Billing administration.\\n\\nThe billable services landing page header is renamed from Billable\\nservices management to Billing administration to match the card, since\\nthe page covers more than billable services. This finishes the rename\\nstarted in #792, which settled on Billing administration as the name\\nfor this area.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"023f5b58f16bced4d5bd551307c298953296be7b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T15:35:51+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Rename billing admin card to Billing administration (#792)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Rename billing admin card to Billing administration\\n\\n* (chore) Sort translation keys\\n\\n* (chore) Include payment modes in billing administration card description\\n\\nThe billing administration view also exposes payment modes configuration,\\nso add it to the card's sub-line.\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"88ef276a8948816911663a855d4e9d9caaec391a\",\"date\":\"2026-06-25T21:08:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Keep the billing form quantity field empty when cleared (#780)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"112a73f7c8a2073efb5ff14f978c7fd11d2b5201\",\"date\":\"2026-06-25T12:33:26+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Keep patient chart siderail visible when launching the billing form (#779)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The \\\"Create bill\\\" and \\\"Add items to bill\\\" actions in the patient chart\\nlaunched the billing form into its own workspace group\\n(billingFormWorkspaceGroup). The workspaces2 system renders only one\\ngroup's action menu at a time, so switching to the billing group dropped\\nthe patient chart's siderail. The billing group defines no window icons\\nof its own, so no siderail rendered in its place either, and the rail\\ndisappeared entirely.\\n\\nRegister a chart-scoped billing form workspace whose window belongs to\\nthe patient-chart group, and launch it from the in-chart call sites\\n(bill history and the bill action menu). The form now opens as a window\\nwithin the patient-chart group, so the group stays active and its\\nsiderail remains visible. The standalone billing pages (invoice,\\nbillable services) continue to use the original billing-form-workspace.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d80cde122d99d7574b754227f40db1c7a4d685cc\",\"date\":\"2026-06-19T13:32:49+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) Refresh billable services table after creating a service (#773)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Refresh billable services table after creating a service\\n\\nCreating a billable service launched the workspace without the\\n`onWorkspaceClose: mutate` callback that the edit path passes, so the\\ntable never revalidated after a create. The only fallback was a global\\n`mutate(url)` in the resource, which is unreliable because the table\\nuses `useOpenmrsFetchAll` (`useSWRInfinite`), whose cache is keyed with\\nan internal `$inf$` prefix and isn't matched by a plain-URL mutate.\\n\\nRoute both create paths (the \\\"Add new service\\\" button and the empty\\nstate) through a single launcher that passes the hook's bound `mutate`\\nas `onWorkspaceClose`, matching the edit path.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Remove ineffective mutate calls from billable service resource\\n\\nThe mutate(url) calls in createBillableService/updateBillableService used\\nthe plain URL, which does not match the $inf$-prefixed aggregated cache key\\nof the useOpenmrsFetchAll (useSWRInfinite) hook backing the table. They never\\nrefreshed the table, and the \\\"Revalidate ... using the exact URL\\\" comments\\nwere misleading. The table refresh is handled by the hook's bound mutate\\npassed as onWorkspaceClose.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HGHCg27zHuJFkgy1JXeQAf\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"bfc75902616d01ad503df362e8c1b84cef60b9dc\",\"date\":\"2026-06-17T18:49:52+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5743: Show an empty state with a Finalize bill action on pending bills (#769)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"90eb9e62b61aa10b96d716902baab4d8408b34de\",\"date\":\"2026-06-15T17:39:16+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5733: Fix squished search bar height in invoice line items table (#767)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"88e4253be27e8917a50de9cf67af37fc5295ab5f\",\"date\":\"2026-06-05T19:56:12+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Isolate BillingDashboard test to prevent unhandled swr error (#759)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e8126b39dc10bcdc719250b004afe86f7782f36a\",\"date\":\"2026-06-04T14:23:05+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5413: Add bill refunds (#738)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat(refunds): add bill refunds feature\\n\\n- Cashiers can request refunds on PAID/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED bills; admins approve or reject; cashiers then process approved refunds to COMPLETED\\n- Supports bill-level and line-item-scoped refunds with cumulative cap enforcement; at most one active refund per scope at a time\\n- Adds admin Refund Requests page, cashier Request Refund modal, and admin Review Bill Refunds modal with receipt rail showing approved and completed refund totals\\n- Fixes: REJECTED refunds were incorrectly reducing remainingRefundable; COMPLETED refunds were not deducted from line-item remaining (double-refund risk); bill.refunds?.filter().reduce() crashed when refunds was undefined\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): add pending refunds filter to bills table\\n\\nAdds REFUND_REQUESTED to BillStatus and a 'Pending refunds' filter option in the bills table to surface bills awaiting refund processing.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): address SonarCloud issues in refunds feature\\n\\n- Extract deeply nested onRefundRequest/onClick callbacks into named functions\\n- Replace chained ternaries with if/else block before JSX return\\n- Add null guard in handleRequestRefund to remove non-null assertions\\n- Use flatMap for type-safe lineItemUuid set construction\\n- Remove unnecessary `as RefundStatus` cast (type already narrows correctly)\\n- Replace role=\\\"progressbar\\\" on div with aria-busy=\\\"true\\\"\\n- Mark component props interfaces as readonly\\n- Replace window with globalThis in test files\\n- Remove unused showSnackbar and useOpenmrsFetchAll imports\\n- Replace parseFloat with Number.parseFloat\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): remove unnecessary non-null assertion in handleLineItemRefundRequest\\n\\nAdd early return guard for item.uuid so TypeScript narrows the type,\\nmaking the ! assertion redundant and satisfying SonarCloud S4325.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): keep review modal open on action and fix multi-line refund eligibility\\n\\n- Review modal now refreshes bill data in place instead of closing after approve/reject\\n- Bills in REFUND_REQUESTED status can now accept refund requests on unaffected line items\\n- Add unit tests covering all refund eligibility scenarios (bill-level and line-level blocking)\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): mock billing.resource in review-bill-refunds modal test\\n\\nuseBill was added to the modal but the test's esm-framework mock did not\\nexpose openmrsFetch, causing the test suite to fail on push.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): resolve duplicate translation key and add voided discount test\\n\\n- Align refundAmount translation value to 'Refund amount' across all usages\\n- Add test asserting voided discounts are not rendered in DiscountsTable\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): add void action to refund review card\\n\\nAdmins can now void any refund regardless of status. Follows the same\\ninline-confirm pattern as the discount card's delete action.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): improve refund review modal and validation\\n\\n- Rename `busy` → `processingRefundId`/`disabled` in RefundCard and RefundReviewStack for clearer semantics\\n- Add per-line-item refund cap validation before approving\\n- Fix over-approval guard to exclude the refund being approved from committed total\\n- Show progress bar alongside content instead of replacing it during loading\\n- Add inline error state when bill data fails to load\\n- Guard against null netAmount in invoice refund handler\\n- Switch requestRefundModal and reviewBillRefundsModal to async lifecycle\\n- Make MappedBill.netAmount non-optional\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): reconcile summary card figures when discount and prior refunds exist\\n\\nShow amountAfterDiscount as the bill-level scope total in the summary card, and\\nadd an 'Already refunded' row (hidden when zero) so all three figures always\\nadd up visually regardless of discounts or prior refunds on the same bill.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Cleanup props\\n\\n* feat(refunds): show tooltip on disabled Request refund button\\n\\nWraps the button in a Carbon Tooltip (only when disabled) to explain\\nthat a line-item refund is already in progress, and adds unit tests\\ncovering the disabled state and tooltip label.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): surface void as delete in UI and add coverage for line-item and void flows\\n\\nReplaces all user-facing \\\"void\\\" language with \\\"delete\\\" to match the\\nconvention used for discounts, line items, and bills. Adds tests for\\nline-item-scoped refund approval (including the exceeds-line-total\\nguard) and the full delete confirmation flow.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): show already-refunded row for line items with prior completed refunds\\n\\nComputes alreadyRefunded symmetrically for line-item refunds using\\nscopeTotal - remainingRefundable, matching the bill-level calculation.\\nThe summary card now shows the \\\"Already refunded\\\" row whenever a line\\nitem has prior completed refunds, making the figures add up correctly.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): close concurrent-action races and i18n gaps\\n\\n- Disable Approve/Confirm reject/Confirm delete across all cards while\\n  any request is in flight (was only guarding the active card's UUID)\\n- Add tests covering cross-card Approve and Confirm-reject lock-out\\n- Remove dead useBillRefunds export and its test block\\n- Add extraction hint block + en.json keys for all BillStatus values\\n  so the receipt-rail status tag never falls back to raw enum strings\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): remove redundant non-null assertions flagged by SonarCloud\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): suppress false invalid state on empty NumberInput on open\\n\\nAdd allowEmpty to the NumberInput in the refund and discount modals so\\nCarbon's internal emptiness check does not trigger the red invalid state\\nbefore the user has typed anything. Submit gating is unaffected.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): keep confirmation footer contained at narrow modal widths\\n\\nSplit confirmation copy from its button group into a wrapping flex row so\\nthe text and controls stack vertically rather than overflow at narrow widths.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2703c255431f8465e8c9f776ae79e601255674bf\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T19:00:15+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5706: Fix paying radio being unclickable when start visit form is opened from appointments page (#751)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4aa8e4c993d5fe06147c9561c949a6da36aea47e\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T17:36:06+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5421: Add visit-bills panel showing visit-scoped bills in visit summary (#741)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat: add visit-bills-panel showing visit-scoped bills in visit summary\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix: address SonarCloud issues in visit-bills-panel\\n\\n- Use stable header.key instead of array index in DataTable header keys\\n- Replace window with globalThis in test setup for env-agnostic access\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix: resolve i18next-parser duplicate key warnings\\n\\n- Use `loadingDescription` for aria-label \\\"Loading\\\" (bills-table, discount-requests)\\n  instead of reusing `loading` with a different default value\\n- Introduce `invoiceNo` key for abbreviated \\\"Invoice #\\\" (discount-requests,\\n  printable-invoice-header) so `invoiceNumber` stays consistently \\\"Invoice number\\\"\\n- Normalise `totalAmount` default to sentence-case \\\"Total amount\\\" in printable invoice\\n- Introduce `deleteBillFailedTryAgain` key for the bill-deletion error message,\\n  separate from the existing line-item-specific `deleteFailedTryAgain`\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(e2e): update invoiceNumberLabel locator to match renamed translation\\n\\nThe `invoiceNumber` key in translations/en.json was changed from \\\"Invoice #\\\"\\nto \\\"Invoice number\\\" in 99a36cc. Update the e2e locator to match.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Bump billing backend dependency and fix stale invoiceNumber translations\\n\\n- Raise backendDependencies billing version to >=2.3.0-0 to include SNAPSHOT builds\\n- Update invoiceNumber label to \\\"Invoice number\\\" across all locale files to align with the invoiceNo/invoiceNumber key split\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (test) Add viewOnly regression tests for InvoiceTable\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (fix) Use getCoreTranslation for loading aria-label in BillsTable\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (fix) Remove redundant progressbar role from BillsTable loader container\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (fix) Remove redundant progressbar role from BillsTable loader container\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Revert non-English translation file changes\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Revert non-English translation file changes\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c08b81ca5f5ca89b434e3f947f47d50cc8bd4b68\",\"date\":\"2026-06-01T11:12:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5714: Only render payment status tag on the chart itself (#749)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3ecce2a55223b21d3c53d4905b346455f94f4fd2\",\"date\":\"2026-05-27T00:18:29+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5705: Use netAmount instead of totalAmount for balance due on printable invoice (#743)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f2616143ab695262370934fe7b74daee40f9c16a\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T23:07:57+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add patient payment status tag to patient banner (#735)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e5b80768f3166c82b2db7c710e166adf01ce3f70\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T01:06:06+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5708: Keep discount review modal open after approve/reject/delete actions (#744)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"8ba8b18ae423df842acd93584f85cafa44577a02\",\"date\":\"2026-05-20T17:59:18+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update BillLineItem type (#733)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"5127b0c031addf584cc49f6252272121d50c5cad\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T22:22:25+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5417: Add bill discounts feature (#732)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add bill discounts feature\\n\\nReplaces bill waivers with a structured discounts workflow:\\n- Per-line-item discount requests via request-discount modal\\n- Discounts table on invoice and printable invoice\\n- Admin dashboard for reviewing pending discount requests\\n- Review-bill-discounts modal with line items, payments, totals,\\n  and receipt rail\\n- Discount entry points wired into invoice page and left-panel\\n- Privilege-aware visibility (useHasPrivilege, feature flag hook)\\n- Server-sourced bill totals via mapBillProperties\\n- BillDiscount type contract and discount resource hooks\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (test) Add e2e tests for bill discounts workflow\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (fix) Update e2e page objects for new invoice layout\\n\\n* (test) Purge bill discounts before bill in e2e cleanup\\n\\n* (test) Skip bill discount e2e pending backend purge support\\n\\nBackend BillDiscountResource.purge throws UnsupportedOperationException, so\\nthe discount workflow spec leaks bills and patients between runs. Skip it and\\ncomment out the discount-cleanup helper until backend purge support lands.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (fix) Address PR review comments on bill discounts\\n\\n- Differentiate Delete button styling from Reject (kind=\\\"danger\\\")\\n- Use custom REST representation instead of v=full for discount requests\\n- Drop redundant optional chaining on bill in payments breakdown\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (fix) Use default rep, memoize modal callbacks, memoize children\\n\\n- Revert custom REST representation to `default` (backend doesn't\\n  serialize nested discount status under custom projections)\\n- Wrap modal handlers in useCallback and children in React.memo\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (fix) Address more PR review comments on bill discounts\\n\\n- Use translation key for Discount requests link title\\n- Drop stale useState snapshot of bill prop in review modal\\n- Preserve non-Error throws in extractErrorMessage fallback\\n- Let InvoiceTable accept discount data as optional props to dedupe fetch with Invoice\\n- Share line item total calculation between modal payload and table row\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"276998ab31efde52652f58a4a22e099970ca615f\",\"date\":\"2026-05-06T03:05:16+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) Default bills table filter to \\\"Pending confirmation\\\" (#727)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"db22701b986ae73bc876df2327fa0f82a7fd3ed5\",\"date\":\"2026-04-22T02:08:55+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add delete action for pending bills (#717)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"311ffcf85b26822b024c384901d45667e680313e\",\"date\":\"2026-04-17T12:46:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Migrate to RSpack and Vitest (#714)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":28}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf239c98-82bb-4f65-bf02-8aacaa0b7f69","uuid":"2fc76b20-3b1f-429d-872e-2e473fef640e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:13:50.929Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c770afca8921295dd87d8e7c185a8a4fef231376\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T18:15:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6112: Create bill / Add bill items workspace should show which patient is being billed in tablet mode (#885)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD\",\"body\":\"* O3-6112: Billing Create bill / Add bill items workspace doesn't show which patient is being billed\\n\\n* O3-6112: Keep billing form fields directly under patient header\\n\\n* (fix) O3-6112: Show patient header in billing form workspace on tablet only\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Juliet wamalwa <julietwamalwa@Juliets-MacBook-Air.local>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0fc74eec7e4432d8ec733c6a9e21f19239ff3740\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T07:47:23+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use the framework PageHeader for the billing headers (#869)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"BillingHeader rebuilt the framework's PageHeader by hand, with its own\\nreceipt illustration, a hardcoded \\\"Billing\\\" label above the title, and\\nthe title in a p. Render PageHeader and PageHeaderContent instead, with\\nthe framework's PaymentsDeskPictogram, so billing picks up the same\\nheader as the rest of O3: the configured implementation name above the\\ntitle, and framework fixes such as the title rendering as a heading.\\n\\nThe billing dashboard's title changes from \\\"Home\\\" to \\\"Billing\\\", since\\n\\\"Billing\\\" no longer appears above it. The administration page keeps\\n\\\"Billing administration\\\". The header doesn't shrink in the\\nadministration page's flex layout, and the unused illustration and\\n\\\"home\\\" translation are removed.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e90bcf41f5e898ad3ca6d32ede21a515a86be639\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T01:24:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Highlight the active billing settings menu item (#874)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Marks the Billing settings submenu item for the current page as active.\\nThe items were never passed `isActive`, so neither Cash point\\nconfiguration nor Payment modes configuration was highlighted while it\\nwas open. The path check is the same one the Billable services,\\nDiscount requests and Refund requests links already use.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d7709b45a79100e07ba5eb03ab0e4a071ae11bb1\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T16:59:54+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Remove leftover workspace v1 container (#857)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Removes the v1 WorkspaceContainer from the billable services home page.\\nThe billing app already uses workspace v2, which the app shell renders on\\nits own, so the container renders nothing today.\\n\\nopenmrs-esm-core#1893 removes WorkspaceContainer from the framework. Once\\nthat ships, the import resolves to undefined and rendering it crashes the\\nbillable services page.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e021519623779cdf5f866fa0541aecfdbcc4aeaa\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T12:05:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Load billing pages, forms and modals only when they open (#854)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Load billing pages, forms and modals only when they open\\n\\nRegister the billing dashboard, billable services page, bill history,\\nvisit check-in form and the seven modals that used getSyncLifecycle with\\ngetAsyncLifecycle instead, so their code only loads when they're shown.\\n\\nWith getSyncLifecycle, all of them were part of the code the module loads\\nas soon as it starts, and the Billing link on the home page starts the\\nmodule. So every session downloaded billing's invoice and forms, along\\nwith zod, react-hook-form and react-to-print, before anyone opened\\nanything billing-related. The module now loads 67 KiB up front instead of\\n297 KiB. The nav links, left panel links and patient banner tags stay\\nsynchronous because they render on other apps' pages.\\n\\n* Share react-router-dom with the app shell\\n\\nAdd react-router-dom to peerDependencies, so billing uses the copy the app\\nshell provides.\\n\\nWithout it, billing bundled and loaded its own copy of react-router-dom,\\nreact-router and @remix-run/router (about 14 KiB), even though the app\\nshell already shares them.\\n\\n* Remove the unused billable services app menu item\\n\\nRemove the billableServicesAppMenuItem extension, its routes.json entry\\nand the menu item component. It was registered in app-menu-item-slot,\\nwhich nothing in the reference application renders. The app menu\\nrenders app-menu-slot, and billable services is still reachable from\\nits System Administration card.\\n\\nThe item was added in #42 for UgandaEMR's app search, which does render\\napp-menu-item-slot, but UgandaEMR now ships its own billing fork\\n(@epcare/esm-billing-app) with its own copy of this extension. The\\n\\\"Billable services\\\" string is still used elsewhere, so the translations\\ndon't change.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6e4cdcd9db634a947b317df793d5b8170a9768e9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T20:43:12+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add date range filter to bills table (#831)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add date range filter to bills table\\n\\n* (feat) Guard inverted date range and show Clear dates only when a date is set\\n\\nSkip the bill fetch when the end date is before the start date and show\\nthe picker's invalid text instead, since the backend rejects that range\\nwith a 400. Render the Clear dates button only when a date is set. Raise\\nthe billing backend floor to 2.5.0-0, which is the version that adds the\\nstartDate and endDate search parameters.\\n\\n* (fix) Skip the bills request for an inverted date range and let the date controls wrap\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"64f5bc47dcd899995e7c60f68712503bc816e939\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T18:39:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Billing app shouldn't generate global CSS rules (#830)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"37f1d48ba37e2e673e90259a086b56ccaf588e81\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T19:12:07+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#808)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace the legacy ESLint configuration with the shared flat config at version 2.0.0. Preserve type-aware export linting and repository-specific rule behavior, remove redundant lint dependencies, and apply the resulting e2e and source cleanups.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4609dcbbcb3a438a135aa3af7c8b0eaf1aa85927\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T02:13:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Shorten the billing admin card copy so it fits its tile\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The billing card on the system administration page used a long\\ndescription, Billable services, cash points, payment modes, discounts,\\nand refunds, as its content line. The admin card tiles have a fixed\\nheight with the arrow icon absolutely positioned in the bottom right\\ncorner, so the three line description overlapped the icon and ran into\\nthe bottom edge of the tile.\\n\\nThe card now follows the pattern the other admin cards use, where the\\nheading is a Manage <domain> category and the content is the name of\\nthe destination: Manage billing over Billing administration.\\n\\nThe billable services landing page header is renamed from Billable\\nservices management to Billing administration to match the card, since\\nthe page covers more than billable services. This finishes the rename\\nstarted in #792, which settled on Billing administration as the name\\nfor this area.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"023f5b58f16bced4d5bd551307c298953296be7b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T15:35:51+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Rename billing admin card to Billing administration (#792)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Rename billing admin card to Billing administration\\n\\n* (chore) Sort translation keys\\n\\n* (chore) Include payment modes in billing administration card description\\n\\nThe billing administration view also exposes payment modes configuration,\\nso add it to the card's sub-line.\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"88ef276a8948816911663a855d4e9d9caaec391a\",\"date\":\"2026-06-25T21:08:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Keep the billing form quantity field empty when cleared (#780)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"112a73f7c8a2073efb5ff14f978c7fd11d2b5201\",\"date\":\"2026-06-25T12:33:26+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Keep patient chart siderail visible when launching the billing form (#779)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The \\\"Create bill\\\" and \\\"Add items to bill\\\" actions in the patient chart\\nlaunched the billing form into its own workspace group\\n(billingFormWorkspaceGroup). The workspaces2 system renders only one\\ngroup's action menu at a time, so switching to the billing group dropped\\nthe patient chart's siderail. The billing group defines no window icons\\nof its own, so no siderail rendered in its place either, and the rail\\ndisappeared entirely.\\n\\nRegister a chart-scoped billing form workspace whose window belongs to\\nthe patient-chart group, and launch it from the in-chart call sites\\n(bill history and the bill action menu). The form now opens as a window\\nwithin the patient-chart group, so the group stays active and its\\nsiderail remains visible. The standalone billing pages (invoice,\\nbillable services) continue to use the original billing-form-workspace.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d80cde122d99d7574b754227f40db1c7a4d685cc\",\"date\":\"2026-06-19T13:32:49+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) Refresh billable services table after creating a service (#773)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Refresh billable services table after creating a service\\n\\nCreating a billable service launched the workspace without the\\n`onWorkspaceClose: mutate` callback that the edit path passes, so the\\ntable never revalidated after a create. The only fallback was a global\\n`mutate(url)` in the resource, which is unreliable because the table\\nuses `useOpenmrsFetchAll` (`useSWRInfinite`), whose cache is keyed with\\nan internal `$inf$` prefix and isn't matched by a plain-URL mutate.\\n\\nRoute both create paths (the \\\"Add new service\\\" button and the empty\\nstate) through a single launcher that passes the hook's bound `mutate`\\nas `onWorkspaceClose`, matching the edit path.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Remove ineffective mutate calls from billable service resource\\n\\nThe mutate(url) calls in createBillableService/updateBillableService used\\nthe plain URL, which does not match the $inf$-prefixed aggregated cache key\\nof the useOpenmrsFetchAll (useSWRInfinite) hook backing the table. They never\\nrefreshed the table, and the \\\"Revalidate ... using the exact URL\\\" comments\\nwere misleading. The table refresh is handled by the hook's bound mutate\\npassed as onWorkspaceClose.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HGHCg27zHuJFkgy1JXeQAf\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"bfc75902616d01ad503df362e8c1b84cef60b9dc\",\"date\":\"2026-06-17T18:49:52+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5743: Show an empty state with a Finalize bill action on pending bills (#769)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"90eb9e62b61aa10b96d716902baab4d8408b34de\",\"date\":\"2026-06-15T17:39:16+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5733: Fix squished search bar height in invoice line items table (#767)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"88e4253be27e8917a50de9cf67af37fc5295ab5f\",\"date\":\"2026-06-05T19:56:12+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Isolate BillingDashboard test to prevent unhandled swr error (#759)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e8126b39dc10bcdc719250b004afe86f7782f36a\",\"date\":\"2026-06-04T14:23:05+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5413: Add bill refunds (#738)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat(refunds): add bill refunds feature\\n\\n- Cashiers can request refunds on PAID/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED bills; admins approve or reject; cashiers then process approved refunds to COMPLETED\\n- Supports bill-level and line-item-scoped refunds with cumulative cap enforcement; at most one active refund per scope at a time\\n- Adds admin Refund Requests page, cashier Request Refund modal, and admin Review Bill Refunds modal with receipt rail showing approved and completed refund totals\\n- Fixes: REJECTED refunds were incorrectly reducing remainingRefundable; COMPLETED refunds were not deducted from line-item remaining (double-refund risk); bill.refunds?.filter().reduce() crashed when refunds was undefined\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): add pending refunds filter to bills table\\n\\nAdds REFUND_REQUESTED to BillStatus and a 'Pending refunds' filter option in the bills table to surface bills awaiting refund processing.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): address SonarCloud issues in refunds feature\\n\\n- Extract deeply nested onRefundRequest/onClick callbacks into named functions\\n- Replace chained ternaries with if/else block before JSX return\\n- Add null guard in handleRequestRefund to remove non-null assertions\\n- Use flatMap for type-safe lineItemUuid set construction\\n- Remove unnecessary `as RefundStatus` cast (type already narrows correctly)\\n- Replace role=\\\"progressbar\\\" on div with aria-busy=\\\"true\\\"\\n- Mark component props interfaces as readonly\\n- Replace window with globalThis in test files\\n- Remove unused showSnackbar and useOpenmrsFetchAll imports\\n- Replace parseFloat with Number.parseFloat\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): remove unnecessary non-null assertion in handleLineItemRefundRequest\\n\\nAdd early return guard for item.uuid so TypeScript narrows the type,\\nmaking the ! assertion redundant and satisfying SonarCloud S4325.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): keep review modal open on action and fix multi-line refund eligibility\\n\\n- Review modal now refreshes bill data in place instead of closing after approve/reject\\n- Bills in REFUND_REQUESTED status can now accept refund requests on unaffected line items\\n- Add unit tests covering all refund eligibility scenarios (bill-level and line-level blocking)\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): mock billing.resource in review-bill-refunds modal test\\n\\nuseBill was added to the modal but the test's esm-framework mock did not\\nexpose openmrsFetch, causing the test suite to fail on push.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): resolve duplicate translation key and add voided discount test\\n\\n- Align refundAmount translation value to 'Refund amount' across all usages\\n- Add test asserting voided discounts are not rendered in DiscountsTable\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): add void action to refund review card\\n\\nAdmins can now void any refund regardless of status. Follows the same\\ninline-confirm pattern as the discount card's delete action.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(refunds): improve refund review modal and validation\\n\\n- Rename `busy` → `processingRefundId`/`disabled` in RefundCard and RefundReviewStack for clearer semantics\\n- Add per-line-item refund cap validation before approving\\n- Fix over-approval guard to exclude the refund being approved from committed total\\n- Show progress bar alongside content instead of replacing it during loading\\n- Add inline error state when bill data fails to load\\n- Guard against null netAmount in invoice refund handler\\n- Switch requestRefundModal and reviewBillRefundsModal to async lifecycle\\n- Make MappedBill.netAmount non-optional\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): reconcile summary card figures when discount and prior refunds exist\\n\\nShow amountAfterDiscount as the bill-level scope total in the summary card, and\\nadd an 'Already refunded' row (hidden when zero) so all three figures always\\nadd up visually regardless of discounts or prior refunds on the same bill.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Cleanup props\\n\\n* feat(refunds): show tooltip on disabled Request refund button\\n\\nWraps the button in a Carbon Tooltip (only when disabled) to explain\\nthat a line-item refund is already in progress, and adds unit tests\\ncovering the disabled state and tooltip label.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): surface void as delete in UI and add coverage for line-item and void flows\\n\\nReplaces all user-facing \\\"void\\\" language with \\\"delete\\\" to match the\\nconvention used for discounts, line items, and bills. Adds tests for\\nline-item-scoped refund approval (including the exceeds-line-total\\nguard) and the full delete confirmation flow.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): show already-refunded row for line items with prior completed refunds\\n\\nComputes alreadyRefunded symmetrically for line-item refunds using\\nscopeTotal - remainingRefundable, matching the bill-level calculation.\\nThe summary card now shows the \\\"Already refunded\\\" row whenever a line\\nitem has prior completed refunds, making the figures add up correctly.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): close concurrent-action races and i18n gaps\\n\\n- Disable Approve/Confirm reject/Confirm delete across all cards while\\n  any request is in flight (was only guarding the active card's UUID)\\n- Add tests covering cross-card Approve and Confirm-reject lock-out\\n- Remove dead useBillRefunds export and its test block\\n- Add extraction hint block + en.json keys for all BillStatus values\\n  so the receipt-rail status tag never falls back to raw enum strings\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): remove redundant non-null assertions flagged by SonarCloud\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): suppress false invalid state on empty NumberInput on open\\n\\nAdd allowEmpty to the NumberInput in the refund and discount modals so\\nCarbon's internal emptiness check does not trigger the red invalid state\\nbefore the user has typed anything. Submit gating is unaffected.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix(refunds): keep confirmation footer contained at narrow modal widths\\n\\nSplit confirmation copy from its button group into a wrapping flex row so\\nthe text and controls stack vertically rather than overflow at narrow widths.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2703c255431f8465e8c9f776ae79e601255674bf\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T19:00:15+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5706: Fix paying radio being unclickable when start visit form is opened from appointments page (#751)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4aa8e4c993d5fe06147c9561c949a6da36aea47e\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T17:36:06+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5421: Add visit-bills panel showing visit-scoped bills in visit summary (#741)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat: add visit-bills-panel showing visit-scoped bills in visit summary\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix: address SonarCloud issues in visit-bills-panel\\n\\n- Use stable header.key instead of array index in DataTable header keys\\n- Replace window with globalThis in test setup for env-agnostic access\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix: resolve i18next-parser duplicate key warnings\\n\\n- Use `loadingDescription` for aria-label \\\"Loading\\\" (bills-table, discount-requests)\\n  instead of reusing `loading` with 